  "diagnosis": "The loop invariants only state that 1 <= i <= a.Length and minVal <= maxVal. They do not relate minVal and maxVal to the actual array elements. At loop exit (i == a.Length), Dafny cannot conclude that minVal is the true minimum or maxVal is the true maximum of the array, so it cannot prove that a[i] - a[j] <= maxVal - minVal for all i, j. The bridge from (invariant ∧ ¬loop_guard) to the postcondition is unprovable without a relational invariant tying minVal/maxVal to the array contents.",
  "repair": "    invariant forall k :: 0 <= k < i ==> minVal <= a[k] && a[k] <= maxVal"
}
